# Postman / API debugging

## Source of truth

- Postman workspace **NutriTrack** (`78e98043-292a-4c10-bed9-f570a3d0c0f5`)
- Collection **NutriTrack Debug** (`a3bff6c0-32f3-492f-ae75-0a68fcce9690`)
- Environment **Railway Production** (`5ef257ec-0c87-4e9b-9690-bb30e916caf8`)
- Details: `AI/production-debug.md`

## When debugging APIs

1. Prefer **gateway** base: `https://gateway-production-777b.up.railway.app`
2. Discover request shapes via Postman MCP (`getCollection` / `getCollectionRequest`), not inventing URLs
3. **Execute** with Shell (`Invoke-RestMethod` / `curl.exe`) — Postman MCP cannot send HTTP
4. Mint tokens with Dev Login:

```json
POST /api/auth/google/callback
{ "code": "dev:agent-debug", "redirectUri": "https://front-end-production-4a95.up.railway.app/auth/callback" }
```

5. Send `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>` on `/api/**` calls
6. On 401: `POST /api/auth/refresh` with `refreshToken`, then retry once

## Prerequisites

- Dev Login works only when auth-service `AUTH_MODE=dev`
- If Railway returns Bad Request on `code: "dev:…"`, ask the user to set `AUTH_MODE=dev` temporarily (or use local compose)
- Prefer gateway over direct service public URLs unless isolating one service

## Do not

- Commit tokens or put secrets in Cypher / search queries
- Call Google OAuth as the agent; use Dev Login instead
- Hit internal `*.railway.internal` hosts from the laptop
